{"reply":"A strong outside lens is Plato’s *Meno*. In that dialogue, Socratic questioning unsettles a person’s confidence in an answer and makes perplexity the beginning of inquiry; the dialogue’s account describes Meno as suddenly unable to speak confidently about virtue after Socrates’ questioning. [Read *Meno* here.](https://gutenberg.org/files/1643/1643-h/1643-h.htm)

That gives the Caterpillar a striking philosophical parallel. In Chapter 5, he begins with the question “Who are _you?_” and keeps returning Alice to it, so that her confusion becomes the subject of the exchange rather than something he immediately resolves. The connection is suggestive, not exact: Socratic perplexity is meant to open a path toward knowledge, while the Caterpillar’s questioning remains enigmatic and offers no clearly constructive follow-through.

So perhaps the useful question is not simply whether the Caterpillar is like Socrates, but whether his calm interrogation helps Alice examine an unstable sense of self—or merely leaves her trapped in confusion. Does his questioning feel to you like the beginning of self-knowledge, or like a test with no fair answer?","evidence_uses":[{"source_kind":"book_corpus","evidence_id":"pg11-v01b38ea4-ch05-ln0960-1016","source_location":"Chapter 5 — Advice from a Caterpillar, source lines 960-1016","exact_quote":"“Who are _you?_”","supported_claims":["In Chapter 5, he begins with the question “Who are _you?_” and keeps returning Alice to it, so that her confusion becomes the subject of the exchange rather than something he immediately resolves."]},{"source_kind":"web","evidence_id":"https://gutenberg.org/files/1643/1643-h/1643-h.htm","exact_quote":null,"supported_claims":["In that dialogue, Socratic questioning unsettles a person’s confidence in an answer and makes perplexity the beginning of inquiry; the dialogue’s account describes Meno as suddenly unable to speak confidently about virtue after Socrates’ questioning."]}],"memory":{"kind":"no_memory_candidate","reason_code":"automatic_capture_disabled"}}

